Lab 2: Maven Integration, Code Review with PMD, and Plugins
-------------------
Areas Covered

Jenkins + Maven Integration.
Build Java project using Maven and Jenkins.
Code review using Maven and Jenkins (PMD).
Maven introduction with plugins/commands.
Poll SCM trigger.
Install plugins in Jenkins.
----------------------

Requirements

Java 17+ and Maven installed on Jenkins (verify: mvn --version).
GitHub repo with a Maven-based Java project (e.g., simple app with pom.xml including PMD plugin).
PMD plugin for Jenkins.
----------------------

Plan of Execution and Guidance

Install Plugins:
Manage Jenkins > Manage Plugins > Available > Search/install: Maven Integration, PMD, Git.
Production Tip: Use a dedicated Jenkins update center mirror for air-gapped environments; audit plugins for vulnerabilities via pluginmanager.jenkins.io.
Maven Project Setup:
Repo pom.xml snippet:XML<build>
    <plugins>
        <plugin>
            <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
            <artifactId>maven-pmd-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>3.21.2</version>
            <executions>
                <execution>
                    <goals><goal>pmd</goal></goals>
                </execution>
            </executions>
        </plugin>
    </plugins>
</build>
Commands to test locally: mvn clean compile and mvn pmd:pmd.
-------------------------------------
Guidance: Ensure src/main/java has sample code with violations (e.g., unused imports) for PMD demo.
-------------------------------------
Create Maven Freestyle Job:
New Item > Maven project > Name: Maven-Java-Build.
Source Management: Git repo URL.
Build Triggers: Poll SCM (H * * * *).
Build: Root POM pom.xml > Goals: clean compile pmd:pmd.
Post-build: Add PMD Publisher (threshold: 0 violations to fail build).
Production Tip: Use Maven's --batch-mode flag in goals for non-interactive CI; cache .m2/repository via workspace retention.
Run and Review:
Build Now > Check console for Maven output.
View PMD report: Job > PMD result link.

Guidance: Introduce a violation (e.g., add import unused;) and push; job should fail with PMD details.
----------------------------------------

Solution

Expected Outcome: Successful Maven build generates target/classes; PMD report highlights violations in HTML/Trend charts.
Verification:
Console Snippet:text[Maven] clean compile pmd:pmd
[INFO] --- maven-pmd-plugin:3.21.2:pmd (default-cli) @ myapp ---
[INFO] Generating "PMD report" report    - 2 violations
PMD Report: Accessible at <job-url>/pmd/, showing file:line violations.

